# Third-party Homebrew entries this repo trusts, applied by `just brew::trust`.
#
# Homebrew 7 will not load a formula or cask from a non-official tap until it is
# trusted, because a formula is arbitrary Ruby that brew executes. The trust
# store (~/.config/homebrew/trust.json under a set XDG_CONFIG_HOME, otherwise
# ~/.homebrew/trust.json) is machine-local and NOT managed by chezmoi, so
# without this file a fresh machine's `brew bundle` fails on every tap below.
#
# This file is the audit trail: trusting something here is a reviewed, committed
# decision rather than an ad-hoc `brew trust` on one box.
#
# Format: <kind> <name>, where kind is tap, formula, or cask.
#
# Prefer `formula`/`cask` over `tap`. A tap entry trusts everything in that
# repo, now and in every future commit; a formula entry is limited to the one
# thing we actually install. Use tap only where the narrower grant will not do.

# workmux (config at home/dot_config/workmux). Single formula, so scope it.
formula raine/workmux/workmux

# AeroSpace (config at home/dot_config/aerospace). Trusted tap-wide: this is a
# cask, and the tap grant is the form already proven to work for it.
tap nikitabobko/tap
